# APKs are too large for a normal git push to GitHub (100MB hard limit).
# Host it as a GitHub Release asset instead and point descargar.html to that URL.
*.apk

# web_export/ ships real narrated audio + story video (~350MB) referenced
# directly by the site at runtime (see js/data.js / js/libro.js / js/paquetes.js).
# Too heavy for a normal git push — host it on real static storage (a CDN
# bucket, GitHub Release asset, etc.) and update the base path in js/data.js
# instead of committing these. The small stuff (data/*.json, laSed_en.txt,
# cover images) stays tracked since it's what makes the content reviewable.
web_export/assets/audio/
web_export/assets/*_stories/*.mp4

# web_export/assets/teoria_videos/ is the opposite case: small enough
# (~38MB total) to actually commit, on purpose -this repo is public, so once
# pushed these are served straight off jsDelivr's GitHub CDN (see the pinned
# commit URL in js/teoria-leccion.js) instead of Firebase Hosting, which
# keeps them off the Hosting storage quota entirely. Tracked, not ignored.

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Firebase CLI local cache (deploy hash cache, not project config)
.firebase/
